% ⚑ THE SAME CLASS AS T12, ONE SCALE UP, AND MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSERTED.
% `_module_edges` holds 15,754 import edges INDEXED ON BOTH COLUMNS
% (reuse_catalog.py:97,112-113) with a `module_edges` view --- so `deps` is
% `ix_medges_src` and `rdeps` is `ix_medges_dst`, and `split_pipeline._import_dag`
% materializes as four eager dicts what the database already serves as seeks.
%
% ⚑ SCOPED, BECAUSE THE TWO SITES ARE NOT THE SAME CASE.  `parse_tree` parses
% SOURCE and is the superset the BUILD GENERATOR requires --- it must emit
% prerequisites for modules that do not compile yet, which a core-derived
% relation cannot cover (2241 distinct src catalogued vs 3457 on disk; 140 cores
% undecodable).  The ANALYSIS consumers have no such requirement.  A verdict
% that lumped them would prescribe deleting the generator's own input.
%
% ⚑ CLOSURE IS DELIBERATELY NOT STORED, and the number is why: sql_lift.py:398
% records the recursive CTE winning ~275x at small N and LOSING at 0.7x at full
% N against eager BFS.  `sqlite_master` holds zero RECURSIVE.  An item that said
% "move the DAG to SQL" would have taken a measured 0.7x regression as progress.
% ⚑ MEASURED, NOT ARGUED: RSS grew 255.3 MB while `tracemalloc` saw 66.2 MB, and
% `gc.collect()` freed 240,279 objects while returning 0.0 MB to the OS.  That is
% cyclic CST garbage recycled into allocator arenas — 2,090,974 `libcst` visit
% calls over 203.9s, per file, per consumer.  The 189.1 MB gap is invisible to
% every allocation-level instrument, which is why four attributions missed it.
%
% ⚑ AND L2 CANNOT FIX IT, BY CONSTRUCTION.  `shared_cache` pickles the WHOLE
% return value under one key (`cached()`: `pickle.dumps(out)`), so a tree fetched
% from it is a tree materialized entire — the same four copies, plus a
% round-trip.  Its docstring is right for what it serves (a comment mask keyed by
% file content is one input, one indivisible output); a CST is not that.
% **A blob store's granularity is the CALL; a table's is the ROW.**
%
% ⚑ THE SCHEMA FITS AS-IS — checked, not assumed.  `_node` carries
% `(kind, role, op)` read as `COALESCE(NULLIF(op,''), role, kind)`: a generic
% three-tier head, not an Agda vocabulary.  `node_child (node_id, ord, child_id)`
% is tree-as-rows with `WHERE ord=0`, `GROUP BY node_id` and `WITH RECURSIVE`
% already in use; `unit_node` is the file->nodes membership; `INSERT OR IGNORE`
% makes it CONTENT-ADDRESSED, so a subtree shared across 747 files is ONE row
% rather than 747 pickles.
%
% ⚑ ONE STORE, NOT TWO (user, 2026-08-04): *"We either reuse the 3.3GB catalog,
% or we stand up ANOTHER sqlite3 file. And we have more mature tooling to work
% with around this one."*  I filed the size as an open question; it is not one.
% A rival store forfeits `catalog_db.connect`, the compiled-builder layer,
% `query_defs --verify` and the drift gate — the four-`agda_files()`-bodies shape
% at the storage layer.
@misc{T30,
  section = {tooling}, from = {T29}, join = {, and },
  claim   = {the Python CST is ingested into catalog.db as interned nodes rather than pickled whole into the shared cache --- a blob store cannot serve a tree piecemeal [cst-blob-sites=0]},
  check   = {item:T30}
}

