  note     = {kind=retraction by=momentum. WHAT IT RETRACTS lived only in prose. I searched for one shape, did not find it, and reported the question unanswered -- before reading the section that answers it from the other direction. A fact about my SEARCH reported as a fact about the CORPUS. NO from EDGE, per the DART reuse-search: supersession is a state rather than an edge between two nodes, and minting the superseded claim purely to be retracted is the entries-whose-only-purpose smell cassian rejects by construction. THE JUSTIFICATION IS THE SIDEWAYS EDGE: presence is not currency, and its converse is what bit here -- absence in the part I read is not absence in the whole, and a needle proves where a reader looked rather than what a corpus holds. Same instrument, same bound, read from the other end.}
}

